  "description": "ZICWUH crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H28 Gd1 Mn4 N4 O20 1-,2(C1 H4 O1),C6 H16 N1 1+,H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 3 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 2 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 3 O neighbors; Mn8 (Mn) has 2 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 1.040-3.901 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 25.99-158.58°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [GdMn4(L1)4(OAc)4]·H4TEA·2MeOH·H2O (anal. C44H54N5Mn4GdO23; H3L1 = salicylhydroxamic acid). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
